#: Game.Levels.LinearIndependenceSpanWorld.Level01
msgid "The first level of this world will introduce the definition of a linear combination. Let's\n"
"say we want to express that some vector §0 is a linear combination of some set §1. This means\n"
"that there is some number of elements in §2, that after some scalar multiplication, sums to §3.\n"
"Since infinite sums are difficult (and sometimes impossible) to work with, we can't simply sum over\n"
"all of §4. Instead, we take some smaller subset §5, with §6, and sum over that.\n"
"Note here the §7 character. This simply takes our finite set §8, which is a §9, and treats it\n"
"as a §10.\n"
"\n"
"Once we have the set we are summing over §11, we need to also multiply the elements of §12 by scalars.\n"
"We do this with a function §13, where each element of §14 gets mapped to the scalar we multiply by.\n"
"Now, we are able to understand the definition of linear combinations:\n"
"\n"
"§15\n"
"\n"
"### The Goal\n"
"The goal of this level is to prove that if §16, then §17 is a linear combination of §18. This can\n"
"be done simply by summing over the set §19, with only multiplying by the scalar 1.\n"
"\n"
"### Defining functions\n"
