#: Game.Levels.InnerProductWorld.Level08
msgid "## Triangle Inequality\n"
"\n"
"In any inner product space, the norm satisfies the triangle inequality:\n"
"§0\n"
"\n"
"Geometrically, this says the straight-line path is the shortest. In this level, you'll prove this fundamental result using the inner product, the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality, and basic algebra.\n"
"\n"
"## Summary\n"
"The triangle inequality is a cornerstone of normed spaces. For any vectors §1 and §2, the straight-line distance (§3) is never greater than the sum of the distances (§4).\n"
"\n"
"## Key idea\n"
"- Expand §5 using the inner product.\n"
"- Use §6 to expand §7.\n"
"- Bound the cross term §8 using the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.\n"
"- Finish by taking square roots, using nonnegativity of norm.\n"
"\n"
"This property is what makes §9 a norm, ensuring our vector space is a metric space!\n"
"\n"
